        "paragraph_id": "3DFA1412",
        "text": "In case of stationary waves Baldock et al. (1998) is applied (keyword: break=baldock), which is presented in (2.14). In this breaking formulation the fraction breaking waves Qb and breaking wave height Hb are calculated differently compared to the breaking formulations used for the non-stationary situation. In (2.14) α is applied as wave dissipation coefficient, frep represents a representative intrinsic frequency and y is a calibration factor."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 14574,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 425,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 357,
        "paragraph_id": "2B2890B4",
        "text": "Finally, it is possible to use the Janssen & Battjes (2007) formulation for wave breaking of stationary waves (keyword: break=janssen). This formulation is a revision of Baldock’s formulation."
      },
      {
